{"cases":[{"attack":false,"case":"","target":"5a74e395ea1b2cadc957188b120fd34288d3704b0829d5ffa24453e1ba45954c"},{"attack":true,"case":"The 'registered attack-defeater' pre-pass operates over defeater edges using a least-fixpoint semantics that is defined independently of the Dung grounded-extension fixed point. When an attack edge is targeted by a defeater warrant whose carrier is not itself attacked by any surviving edge, the edge is removed in a monotone least-fixpoint over the defeater subgraph; only afterward does the standard Dung grounded extension run on the surviving graph. This composes TWO fixed points (defeater-pre-pass + grounded extension) rather than deriving reinstatement from a single skeptical fixed-point semantics. The problem requires that proposals preserve reinstatement as 'a derived property of the same fixpoint'; here reinstatement of an argument whose attacker was defeated arises from the separate defeater pre-pass, not from the grounded-extension fixpoint itself, so the guarantee is not preserved as stated.","target":"a82bea5b945bd5205c1a11272a3ddf8bfdd103abe7bbda429828f4707b431110"}]}